# G9 (graphics): the pointer in the file dialog's Save As and the boxes over it. New folder opens its box and Cancel closes it, OK with
# no name says so and OK on the notice closes that, a read-only file is refused, a name that is there asks before it is replaced and
# No keeps the dialog, Cancel ends it, and Yes saves. Every frame's CRC-32 must equal the host's in both graphics modes.
@dialog
@dir QUILL
@place Quill C:\QUILL
@cwd C:\DOCS
@copy letter.qld DOCS\
@copy letter.rtf DOCS\
@copy plain.qld DOCS\
@stamp DOCS\LETTER.QLD 2026-11-24 18:45
@stamp DOCS\LETTER.RTF 2026-11-02 09:05
@stamp DOCS\PLAIN.QLD 2026-03-14 12:00
@readonly DOCS\PLAIN.QLD
@open C:\DOCS\LETTER.QLD
f10 down down down enter      # File > Save As...
@click 460 83                 # New folder: its box
@click 560 83
@click 312 270                # Cancel: the box closes
@click 460 83
@click 232 270                # OK with no name: a notice
@click 185 280                # OK
@click 312 270                # Cancel
@click 200 159                # PLAIN.QLD
@click 490 391                # Save: it is read-only
@click 185 280                # OK
@click 500 369                # the type drop-down
@click 500 334                # Rich Text Format: LETTER.RTF is listed
@click 200 143                # LETTER.RTF
@click 490 391                # Save: it is there, so it asks
@click 262 280                # No
@click 580 391                # Cancel: the dialog ends
f10 down down down enter
@click 500 369
@click 500 334
@click 200 143
@click 490 391
@click 185 280                # Yes: saved
